    body:
      "## New York in May 2025\n\nNew York was one of those places that had always felt larger than life to me. It is the kind of city you grow up seeing in movies, photos, and random references everywhere, so being there in person almost felt unreal.\n\nIn May 2025, I spent a week living in Manhattan, and the whole experience felt a little dreamlike. The city moves fast. There are always people walking, taxis passing, lights everywhere, and something happening on every street. At first it feels overwhelming, but after a while it becomes exciting. Even simple walks started to feel cinematic.\n\n## Living in Manhattan\n\nSpending a week in Manhattan felt surreal. There was always something happening, and even regular walks felt interesting. The city had this energy that made everything feel alive.\n\nSome of my favorite moments were not even planned. Just walking around, looking at buildings, people-watching, and taking in the atmosphere made the trip special.\n\nOne thing that stood out to me across all of New York was the food. It felt like there were endless options everywhere. There were food chains, cafes, dessert places, and restaurants on almost every block.\n\nI love trying new foods and cuisines, so this was one of my favorite parts of the trip. New York felt like the kind of place where you could try something new every day and still leave with more places on your list.\n\n[image:travel-nyc-food.png|Trying new food was one of my favorite parts of being in New York.]\n\n## Why SoHo Was My Favorite\n\nEven though I liked a lot of different parts of the city, SoHo was definitely my favorite. I loved its vibe. It felt stylish, designer, and full of personality. There was something about it that felt polished and effortless at the same time.\n\nIt was one of those places where I enjoyed just walking around without any plan and taking everything in.\n\n## A Very Impulsive Decision\n\nSomewhere in the middle of the trip, I made a completely impulsive decision and got bangs for the first time.\n\nIt felt like the kind of thing that only makes sense when you are in New York. Very random, very impulsive, but also very memorable.\n\n[image:travel-nyc-bangs.jpg|New city, new bangs.]\n\n## The Classic New York Moments\n\nThere were also a lot of those moments that felt very New York.\n\nI saw the Statue of Liberty, visited the Vessel, went to the harbourfront, and took a boat that passed under the Brooklyn Bridge. Being on the water and seeing the skyline from that angle made the city feel even more unreal.\n\n[image:travel-nyc-statue.jpg|Seeing the Statue of Liberty in person was one of those moments that did not feel real until it happened.]\n\nI also went to Bryant Park, where my cousin and I made bracelets at an art cart, which ended up being one of the sweetest little memories from the trip.\n\n## Museums and Places\n\nI visited MoMA and also saw a Picasso painting in person for the first time. Picasso is not someone I personally care deeply about, but it still felt nice to finally see something so famous in real life after hearing about it for so many years.\n\n## What I Did Not Like\n\nNot everything was my favorite, though. I did not like the subway. It was one of the few parts of the trip that I did not enjoy much.\n\n## Looking Back\n\nThe week went by quickly, but it felt full of little moments that made it memorable. Exploring Manhattan, trying new food, spending time in SoHo, visiting museums, seeing iconic places, making bracelets in Bryant Park, and doing something spontaneous like getting bangs all made the trip feel special.\n\nNew York felt exciting, overwhelming, stylish, and unforgettable all at once.\n\nAnd for one week, living in Manhattan felt like stepping into a world I had only imagined before.",
